{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:ab6ab4ebec5ca618","name":"Anjiliac Thug","source":{"id":"source:reference-ab6ab4ebec5ca618","title":"Anjiliac Thug","revision":15834,"timestamp":"2024-08-18T00:53:17Z","sha256":"10a9ce3da3e554f4748f85b3623116abc107416bb7bb2a11dab081e107a0d75e","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=15834","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Anjiliac%20Thug&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-ab6ab4ebec5ca618","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scum and Villainy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scum_and_Villainy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Anjiliac Kajidic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Anjiliac_Kajidic","referenceId":"reference:d6ea372a77f73637"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["The Hutt Kajidics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Hutt_Kajidics","referenceId":"reference:3f107406b356c3df"},", including the Desilijic Kajidic, employ ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gamorreans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gamorreans"}," as thugs, but ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Anjiliac Kajidic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Anjiliac_Kajidic","referenceId":"reference:d6ea372a77f73637"}," has a preference for using ",{"tag":"a","children":["Houk"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Houk","referenceId":"reference:851e48cea0867fb9"},". Given the Houk's sinister reputation for foul tempers and raw physical strength, their presence on behalf of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Zietta the Hutt"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Zietta_the_Hutt","referenceId":"reference:52cd14151df89b2e"}," in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Point Nadir"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Point_Nadir","referenceId":"reference:480bbe618709d93f"}," often ends a confrontation before it can begin. This suits the Anjiliacs just fine, but it has an undesirable effect on the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Houk"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Houk","referenceId":"reference:851e48cea0867fb9"},", who take out their aggressions on less-deserving targets in their spare time.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Houk"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Houk","referenceId":"reference:851e48cea0867fb9"}," can be found nearly everywhere in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Point Nadir"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Point_Nadir","referenceId":"reference:480bbe618709d93f"},", with at least eighty of them on the Anjiliac payroll. They wander the shadowport in groups of two to five, looking for trouble. If they are unable to find conflict, they are always willing to generate some of their own. The typical Anjiliac Houk wears a pair of well-worn ",{"tag":"a","children":["Combat Gloves"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Combat_Gloves","referenceId":"reference:2bd4897a780f381e"},", and carries a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vibro-Axe"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vibro-Axe","referenceId":"reference:b56c1438f36d66b7"}," and a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Blaster Carbine"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Blaster_Carbine","referenceId":"reference:76b5919337653c76"},", as well as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Blaster Pistol"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Blaster_Pistol","referenceId":"reference:38dcc06542ba096c"}," \"just in case.\" \n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Anjiliac Thug Statistics (CL 3)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Houk"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Houk","referenceId":"reference:851e48cea0867fb9"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 3/",{"tag":"a","children":["Soldier"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Soldier","referenceId":"reference:f826baa05bef6921"}," 2\n"]